LANG_DATA['alq'].meta = { family: 'Algonquian (Anishinaabemowin)', speakers: '~2.5K', countries: 'Canada (Quebec — Abitibi, Outaouais; Ontario — Pikwakanagan, Timiskaming)', official: 'No (recognized Indigenous language of Canada)', script: 'Latin (with grave accent à è ì ò for long vowels)', iso6393: 'alq', glottocode: 'algo1255', dataStatus: 'fragmentary', reviewStatus: 'human-reviewed', scriptTags: ['Latin'], unattestedReason: { cat: 'unsourced' }, sources: [{ type: 'reference', title: 'McGregor, Ernest (1987) Algonquin Lexicon. River Desert Education Authority, Maniwaki.' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Cuoq, Jean-André (1886) Lexique de la langue algonquine. Dawson Bros., Montréal.' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Daviault, Diane (1994) L\'algonquin au XVIIe siècle. Presses de l\'Université du Québec.' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Glottolog: Algonquin', url: 'https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/algo1255' }], description: { en: 'Easternmost variety of the Anishinaabemowin (Ojibwe) dialect continuum, spoken along the Ottawa River watershed. Distinguished from western Ojibwe by retention of /n/ where other varieties show /h/ or zero, and by heavy French lexical influence in modern speech.', ja: 'アニシナベモウィン（オジブウェ）方言連続体の最東端の変種で、オタワ川流域で話される。西方オジブウェが /h/ または無音を示す位置に /n/ を保つ点、および現代語のフランス語借用の多さで区別される。', ko: '아니시나베모윈(오지브웨) 방언 연속체의 최동단 변종으로 오타와강 유역에서 사용된다. 서부 오지브웨가 /h/ 또는 무음을 보이는 자리에서 /n/을 유지하며, 현대어에 프랑스어 차용이 많은 점에서 구별된다.', zh: '阿尼希纳贝莫温（奥吉布瓦）方言连续体最东端的变体，分布于渥太华河流域。在西部奥吉布瓦失落或弱化为 /h/ 的位置仍保留 /n/，且现代口语中含大量法语借词，与其他变体明显不同。' } };
LANG_DATA['ckv'].meta = { family: 'Austronesian (East Formosan)', speakers: '~24 (critically endangered; revival underway)', countries: 'Taiwan (Yilan, Hualien)', official: 'Yes (one of 16 recognized indigenous languages of Taiwan since 2002)', script: 'Latin (Council of Indigenous Peoples orthography)', iso6393: 'ckv', glottocode: 'kava1241', dataStatus: 'fragmentary', reviewStatus: 'human-reviewed', scriptTags: ['Latin'], unattestedReason: { love: 'unsourced', heart: 'unsourced', hello: 'unsourced', thanks: 'unsourced', good: 'unsourced' }, sources: [{ type: 'reference', title: 'Li, Paul Jen-kuei & Tsuchida, Shigeru (2006) Kavalan Dictionary. Institute of Linguistics, Academia Sinica, Taipei.' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Li, Paul Jen-kuei & Tsuchida, Shigeru (2006) Kavalan Texts. Academia Sinica.' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Glottolog: Kavalan', url: 'https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/kava1241' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Council of Indigenous Peoples (Taiwan): Kebalan / Kavalan language resources', url: 'https://www.cip.gov.tw/' }], description: { en: 'Kavalan (Kebalan) is a critically endangered East Formosan Austronesian language of eastern Taiwan, with only around two dozen fluent elderly speakers concentrated in Hualien (Sinshe/Paterungan villages) and remembered in Yilan. Officially recognized as a separate Indigenous people of Taiwan in 2002 after a long campaign. Typologically conservative within Austronesian: retains Proto-Austronesian *R as /x/ (e.g. zanuR > zanum-related cognates), preserves a four-way Philippine-type voice system, and shows VOS basic order. Revitalization efforts include the CIP "Language Nest" program.', ja: 'カバラン語（Kebalan）は台湾東部の絶滅危機にある東フォルモサ系オーストロネシア言語で、流暢な高齢話者は花蓮（新社・パテルンガン集落）と宜蘭の記憶話者を合わせても約24名に過ぎない。長年の運動の末、2002年に台湾の独立した原住民族として正式に認定された。オーストロネシア諸語の中では類型的に保守的で、古オーストロネシア祖語 *R を /x/ として保持し、フィリピン型の4焦点ヴォイス体系を備え、基本語順は VOS。原住民族委員会の「語言巣（言語の巣）」プログラムによる継承運動が進む。', ko: '카발란어(Kebalan)는 대만 동부의 동포모사계 오스트로네시아 언어로 심각한 절멸 위기에 있으며, 유창한 고령 화자는 화롄(신서·파테룽안 마을)과 이란을 합쳐 약 24명에 불과하다. 오랜 운동 끝에 2002년 대만의 독립된 원주민족으로 공식 인정되었다. 오스트로네시아 제어 중 유형적으로 보수적이며 원시 오스트로네시아조어 *R을 /x/로 보존하고, 필리핀형 4초점 보이스 체계를 유지하며 기본 어순은 VOS. 원주민족 위원회의 "언어 둥지(語言巢)" 프로그램을 통한 부흥 운동이 진행 중.', zh: '噶玛兰语（Kebalan）是台湾东部濒危的东台湾南岛语言，流利的高龄使用者集中于花莲（新社、Paterungan 部落）和宜兰回忆者合计仅约24人。经长期运动，2002年正式获认定为台湾独立原住民族。在南岛诸语中类型上保守，保留原始南岛语 *R 为 /x/，保有菲律宾型四焦点语态体系，基本语序为 VOS。原住民族委员会"语言巢"计画推动语言复振。' } };
LANG_DATA['haj'].meta = { family: 'Indo-Aryan (Eastern; Bengali-Assamese contact zone)', speakers: '~70K', countries: 'India (Meghalaya, Assam) and Bangladesh (Mymensingh, Netrokona)', official: 'No (Scheduled Tribe language in India; not constitutionally listed)', script: 'Bengali / Eastern Nagari (also Assamese alphabet; Latin used in linguistic work)', iso6393: 'haj', glottocode: 'hajo1238', dataStatus: 'fragmentary', reviewStatus: 'human-reviewed', scriptTags: ['Bengali', 'Latin'], unattestedReason: { cat: 'unsourced', love: 'unsourced', hello: 'unsourced', thanks: 'unsourced' }, sources: [{ type: 'reference', title: 'van Driem, George (2001) Languages of the Himalayas. Brill, Leiden — entry on Hajong.' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Phillips, Vivian C. (2011) Sino-Tibetan elements in Hajong. SIL Electronic Survey Report.' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Grierson, G. A. (1903) Linguistic Survey of India, Vol. V Part I — Hajong vocabulary.' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Glottolog: Hajong', url: 'https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/hajo1238' }], description: { en: 'Hajong is an Eastern Indo-Aryan language of the Hajong people in the Garo Hills (Meghalaya, India) and adjacent Bangladesh. Lexically Indo-Aryan and closely allied to Bengali-Assamese, it shows heavy contact influence from neighbouring Tibeto-Burman Garo, and is unusual for an Indo-Aryan language in being written in both Bengali and Assamese alphabets by its speakers.', ja: 'ハジョン語はインド・メーガーラヤ州ガロ丘陵および隣接バングラデシュのハジョン族が話す東部インド・アーリア語。語彙的にはベンガル・アッサム語に近いが、隣接するチベット・ビルマ語派のガロ語からの強い接触影響を受けており、ベンガル文字とアッサム文字の両方で書かれる点でインド・アーリア語としては珍しい。', ko: '하종어는 인도 메갈라야 가로 구릉 및 인접 방글라데시의 하종족이 사용하는 동부 인도아리아어이다. 어휘는 벵골·아삼어에 가깝지만 인접한 티베트버마계 가로어의 강한 접촉 영향을 받았으며, 인도아리아어로는 드물게 벵골 문자와 아삼 문자 양쪽으로 표기된다.', zh: '哈絨語為印度梅加拉亞邦加羅丘陵及鄰近孟加拉哈絨人所操之東部印度－雅利安語。詞彙近於孟加拉－阿薩姆語，但深受鄰近藏緬語族加羅語接觸影響；於印雅語中罕見地同時使用孟加拉文與阿薩姆文書寫。' } };
LANG_DATA['kzj'].meta = { family: 'Austronesian (Dusunic, Sabahan)', speakers: '~150K', countries: 'Malaysia (Sabah, Penampang district)', official: 'No (recognized indigenous language of Sabah; KDCA standard alongside Central Dusun)', script: 'Latin', iso6393: 'kzj', glottocode: 'coas1294', reviewStatus: 'human-reviewed', scriptTags: ['Latin'], sources: [{ type: 'reference', title: 'Hurlbut, Hope M. (1988) Verb morphology in Eastern Kadazan. Pacific Linguistics B-97, ANU.' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Miller, Carolyn P. & Miller, John D. (1991) Kadazan/Dusun phonology revisited. Pacific Linguistics A-78.' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Glottolog: Coastal Kadazan', url: 'https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/coas1294' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Ethnologue 27: Kadazan, Coastal', url: 'https://www.ethnologue.com/language/kzj/' }], description: { en: 'Coastal Kadazan (autonym Boos Momogun) is the Dusunic Austronesian language of Penampang and Papar on the west coast of Sabah, distinct from the inland Central Dusun (dtp) cluster though mutually partly intelligible and unified under the KDCA literary standard. Uses a five-vowel system with phonemic /v/ (a typological rarity in Sabahan), and like other Dusunic languages has a rich Philippine-type voice system (actor/patient/locative/instrumental focus). Penampang is the cultural heartland of the Kaamatan harvest festival.', ja: '沿岸カダザン語（自称 Boos Momogun）はサバ州西岸ペナンパン・パパール地区のドゥスン系オーストロネシア言語で、内陸の中部ドゥスン語（dtp）群とは別個ながら部分的に相互理解可能で、KDCA文学標準の下に統合される。5母音体系で音素 /v/ を持つ点はサバ系言語として類型的に珍しい。他のドゥスン諸語と同じくフィリピン型のヴォイス体系（動作者・被動者・場所・道具焦点）を持つ。ペナンパンはカマタン収穫祭の文化的中心地。', ko: '연안 카다잔어(자칭 Boos Momogun)는 사바 주 서해안 페남팡·파파르 지구의 두순계 오스트로네시아 언어로, 내륙 중부 두순어(dtp)군과 별개이지만 부분적으로 상호 이해 가능하며 KDCA 문학 표준 아래 통합된다. 5모음 체계에 음소 /v/를 가지며 이는 사바계 언어로서 유형론적으로 드물다. 다른 두순계 언어와 마찬가지로 필리핀형 보이스 체계(행위자·피동작·장소·도구 초점)를 갖는다. 페남팡은 카아마탄 추수 축제의 문화적 중심지.', zh: '沿海卡达赞语（自称 Boos Momogun）是沙巴州西海岸槟南邦和巴巴区的杜顺系南岛语言，与内陆中部杜顺语（dtp）群体相区别，但部分互通，统一在 KDCA 文学标准之下。具有五元音系统及音位 /v/，这在沙巴系语言中类型上较为罕见。与其他杜顺语一样具有菲律宾型语态系统（施事/受事/处所/工具焦点）。槟南邦是卡阿玛丹丰收节的文化中心地。' } };
LANG_DATA['mez'].meta = { family: 'Algonquian (Central)', speakers: '~35 L1 + revitalization L2', countries: 'USA (Wisconsin — Menominee Reservation)', official: 'Yes (official language of the Menominee Indian Tribe of Wisconsin)', script: 'Latin (Bloomfield/Miner orthography with macron + q for glottal stop)', iso6393: 'mez', glottocode: 'meno1252', dataStatus: 'fragmentary', reviewStatus: 'human-reviewed', scriptTags: ['Latin'], unattestedReason: { cat: 'unsourced', thanks: 'unsourced' }, sources: [{ type: 'reference', title: 'Bloomfield, Leonard (1962) The Menomini Language. Yale University Press.' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Bloomfield, Leonard (1975) Menomini Lexicon (ed. Charles Hockett). Milwaukee Public Museum.' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Glottolog: Menominee', url: 'https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/meno1252' }], description: { en: 'Sole isolate within Central Algonquian — Menominee diverged early and shares no close sister inside its branch. Notable for its four-vowel system with phonemic length and a complex direct/inverse verb morphology typical of Algonquian.', ja: '中央アルゴンキン諸語の孤立的支系で、近縁の姉妹語を持たない。母音長の音素的対立を持つ4母音体系と、アルゴンキン特有の直接/逆方向動詞形態論で知られる。', ko: '중앙 알공킨어군 내에서 가장 일찍 분기한 고립 분파로, 가까운 자매 언어가 없다. 음소적 모음 길이를 가진 4모음 체계와 알공킨어 특유의 직접/역방향 동사 형태론이 특징이다.', zh: '中阿尔冈昆语群中早期分化的孤立分支，无近亲姊妹语言。具有音位性元音长度的四元音系统，以及阿尔冈昆语族典型的直接/反向动词形态。' } };
LANG_DATA['nan_xm'].meta = { family: 'Sino-Tibetan (Sinitic, Min Nan, Quanzhang/Hokkien)', speakers: '~3M', countries: 'China (Xiamen/Amoy, Fujian)', official: 'No (recognized regional)', script: 'Han characters / Pe̍h-ōe-jī romanization', iso6393: 'nan', glottocode: 'xiam1236', reviewStatus: 'human-reviewed', scriptTags: ['Hans', 'Latin'], sources: [{ type: 'reference', title: 'Douglas, Carstairs (1873) Chinese-English Dictionary of the Vernacular or Spoken Language of Amoy. London: Trübner.' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Wikipedia: Amoy dialect', url: 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amoy_dialect' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Glottolog: Xiamen', url: 'https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/xiam1236' }], description: { en: 'Xiamen Hokkien (厦门话, "Amoy") is the prestige Quanzhang variety of Min Nan spoken by ~3M in the Xiamen metropolitan area of southern Fujian. Historically the most influential Min Nan dialect: it formed as a koine blending Quanzhou and Zhangzhou features after Xiamen\'s 19th-century opening as a treaty port, and became the de facto standard for Western missionary linguistics — Douglas\' 1873 dictionary and the entire Pe̍h-ōe-jī romanization tradition are based on it. The Amoy koine is also the historical seed of modern Taiwanese Hokkien, which descends directly from 17th–19th century Quanzhou-Zhangzhou settler dialects mixed in the same way.', ja: '厦門語（Amoy、厦门话）は福建省南部の厦門都市圏で約300万人が話す閩南語泉漳片の威信変種である。歴史的に最も影響力のある閩南語方言で、19世紀の条約港開港後に泉州・漳州の特徴を融合して成立したコイネーであり、ダグラス（1873）辞書および白話字（Pe̍h-ōe-jī）ローマ字伝統など西洋宣教言語学の事実上の標準形となった。同じく17–19世紀の泉漳系移民言語が混成して成立した現代台湾閩南語の歴史的母体でもある。', ko: '샤먼 민난어（Amoy, 厦门话）는 푸젠 남부 샤먼 도시권에서 약 300만 명이 사용하는 민난어 취안장(泉漳) 위신 변종이다. 역사적으로 가장 영향력 있는 민난어 방언으로, 19세기 조약항 개항 이후 취안저우·장저우 특징을 융합하여 형성된 코이네이며, 더글러스(1873) 사전과 백화자(Pe̍h-ōe-jī) 로마자 전통 등 서양 선교 언어학의 사실상 표준이 되었다. 동일한 방식으로 17–19세기 취안·장 이민 방언이 혼합되어 형성된 현대 대만 민난어의 역사적 모태이기도 하다.', zh: '厦门话（Amoy、闽南语泉漳片威信变体）通行于福建南部厦门都会区，使用人口约300万。是历史上影响力最大的闽南语方言：19世纪厦门开埠为条约港后，融合泉州、漳州特征形成的「厦门腔」共同语，并成为西方传教士语言学的事实标准——道格拉斯（1873）字典及整个白话字（Pe̍h-ōe-jī）罗马字传统皆以厦门音为基础。同样混合自17–19世纪泉漳移民方言的现代台湾闽南语，其历史源头亦在厦门腔。' } };
LANG_DATA['nan_zz'].meta = { family: 'Sino-Tibetan (Sinitic, Min Nan, Quanzhang/Hokkien)', speakers: '~10M (Zhangzhou prefecture and diaspora)', countries: 'China (Zhangzhou, Fujian)', official: 'No (recognized regional)', script: 'Han characters / Pe̍h-ōe-jī romanization', iso6393: 'nan', glottocode: 'zhan1242', reviewStatus: 'human-reviewed', scriptTags: ['Hans', 'Latin'], sources: [{ type: 'reference', title: 'Zhou Changji 周長楫 (1996) 闽南方言大词典 [Great Dictionary of the Min Nan Dialect]. Fujian People\'s Publishing House.' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Wikipedia: Zhangzhou dialect', url: 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zhangzhou_dialect' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Glottolog: Zhangzhou', url: 'https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/zhan1242' }], description: { en: 'Zhangzhou Hokkien (漳州话) is one of the two parent dialects of the entire Quanzhang/Hokkien branch of Min Nan, spoken by ~10M across Zhangzhou prefecture in southern Fujian and a substantial overseas diaspora. The classic Quanzhou-vs-Zhangzhou split underlies all later Hokkien koines: Xiamen and Taiwanese both arose as Quanzhou-Zhangzhou mixed varieties. Zhangzhou-leaning features (notably the -uiⁿ vowels and a "softer" tone contour) are still identifiable in Taiwanese sub-dialects of southern Taiwan (e.g. Tainan), while Quanzhou-leaning features dominate northern Taiwan (e.g. Lukang).', ja: '漳州語（Zhangzhou Hokkien、漳州话）は閩南語泉漳片の二大祖方言のひとつで、福建省南部の漳州市と多数の海外華人社会で約1,000万人に話される。泉州方言と漳州方言の古典的な対立はすべての後世の閩南語コイネーの基層をなし、厦門語・台湾語はいずれも両方言の混合として成立した。漳州的特徴（-uiⁿ韻、より柔らかい声調曲線など）は南部台湾の台湾語下位方言（台南など）に今も識別可能であり、北部台湾（鹿港など）では泉州的特徴が優勢である。', ko: '장저우 민난어（Zhangzhou Hokkien, 漳州话）는 민난어 취안장(泉漳)계의 두 모방언 중 하나로, 푸젠 남부 장저우 지역과 다수의 화교 사회에서 약 1,000만 명이 사용한다. 취안저우·장저우의 고전적 대립은 이후 모든 민난어 코이네의 기층을 이루며, 샤먼어와 대만어는 모두 양 방언의 혼합으로 형성되었다. 장저우계 특징(-uiⁿ 운, 보다 부드러운 성조 곡선 등)은 남부 대만 민난어 하위방언(타이난 등)에서 식별 가능하며, 북부 대만(루강 등)에서는 취안저우계 특징이 우세하다.', zh: '漳州话（漳州闽南语）是闽南语泉漳片的两大母方言之一，通行于福建南部漳州市及大量海外华人社群，使用人口约1,000万。泉州、漳州两方言的古典对立构成日后所有闽南语共同语的底层——厦门话与台湾话皆为两腔混合的产物。漳州倾向特征（-uiⁿ 韵母、声调曲线较柔等）至今可在台湾南部闽南语次方言（如台南腔）中识别，而台湾北部（如鹿港）则以泉州倾向特征为主。' } };
LANG_DATA['osa'].meta = { family: 'Siouan (Dhegihan)', speakers: '~15 L1 + active revitalization L2', countries: 'USA (Oklahoma — Osage Nation, Pawhuska)', official: 'Yes (official language of the Osage Nation)', script: 'Osage script (developed 2006 by Herman Mongrain Lookout, Unicode 9.0 / 2016); also Latin orthography', iso6393: 'osa', glottocode: 'osag1243', reviewStatus: 'human-reviewed', scriptTags: ['Osge', 'Latin'], sources: [{ type: 'reference', title: 'Quintero, Carolyn (2004) Osage Grammar. University of Nebraska Press.' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Quintero, Carolyn (2009) Osage Dictionary. University of Oklahoma Press.' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'LaFlesche, Francis (1932) A Dictionary of the Osage Language. Smithsonian BAE Bulletin 109.' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Glottolog: Osage', url: 'https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/osag1243' }], description: { en: 'Dhegihan Siouan language closely related to Kansa, Quapaw, and Omaha-Ponca. Uniquely among Indigenous North American languages, Osage uses its own purpose-built alphabet (the Osage script, 𐓏𐓘𐓻𐓘𐓻𐓟) created by Herman Mongrain Lookout in 2006 and officially adopted by the Osage Nation in 2014.', ja: 'デガハ系スー語族に属し、カンザ語・クアパウ語・オマハ＝ポンカ語と近縁。北米先住民言語としては珍しく、ハーマン・モングラン・ルックアウトが2006年に創案し2014年にオセージ民族が公式採用した独自のオセージ文字（𐓏𐓘𐓻𐓘𐓻𐓟）を用いる。', ko: '데가하 수어족 언어로 칸자어·콰파우어·오마하-폰카어와 가깝다. 북미 토착어로는 드물게, 허먼 몽그레인 룩아웃이 2006년에 만들고 2014년 오세이지 부족이 공식 채택한 독자 문자(오세이지 문자, 𐓏𐓘𐓻𐓘𐓻𐓟)를 사용한다.', zh: '德加哈苏语支语言，与堪萨语、夸保语、奥马哈—庞卡语近缘。在北美原住民语言中独具特色，使用赫尔曼·蒙格兰·卢克奥特于2006年创制、奥塞奇民族于2014年正式采用的专属字母（奥塞奇文字 𐓏𐓘𐓻𐓘𐓻𐓟）。' } };
LANG_DATA['pgz'].meta = { family: 'Austronesian (Malayic creole / Eastern Malay)', speakers: '~1M (L1+L2)', countries: 'Indonesia (Papua, West Papua provinces)', official: 'No (lingua franca; Indonesian remains national official)', script: 'Latin', iso6393: 'pgz', glottocode: 'papu1250', reviewStatus: 'human-reviewed', scriptTags: ['Latin'], sources: [{ type: 'reference', title: 'Kluge, Angela (2014) A grammar of Papuan Malay. Language Science Press.' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Glottolog: Papuan Malay', url: 'https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/papu1250' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Ethnologue 27: Papuan Malay', url: 'https://www.ethnologue.com/language/pgz/' }], description: { en: 'Papuan Malay is the eastern-Indonesian Malay-based contact language and lingua franca of the western half of New Guinea, structurally simplified relative to standard Indonesian (no voice-marking morphology, reduced affixation, preposed possessor "sa pu rumah" = "my house"). Distinct enough from Bahasa Indonesia that Kluge (2014) treats it as a separate language rather than a dialect. Carries strong substrate influence from local Papuan and Austronesian languages of the Cenderawasih Bay region.', ja: 'パプア・マレー語はニューギニア島西半部（インドネシア領パプア）のリンガフランカで、マレー語を基盤とする東インドネシアの接触言語。標準インドネシア語に比べ態の形態論を欠き、接辞が大幅に縮小され、所有者が前置される（sa pu rumah「私の家」）など構造的に単純化されている。クルーゲ（2014）はインドネシア語の方言ではなく独立した言語として扱う。チェンデラワシ湾地域のパプア諸語・オーストロネシア諸語の基層を強く受ける。', ko: '파푸아 말레이어는 뉴기니섬 서반부(인도네시아령 파푸아)의 링구아 프랑카로, 말레이어를 기반으로 한 동인도네시아 접촉어. 표준 인도네시아어에 비해 태(voice) 형태론이 없고 접사가 축소되었으며 소유자가 선행한다(sa pu rumah "내 집"). Kluge(2014)는 인도네시아어의 방언이 아닌 별개 언어로 다룬다. 첸데라와시 만 지역의 파푸아·오스트로네시아 기층 영향이 강하다.', zh: '巴布亚马来语是新几内亚西半部（印尼属巴布亚）的通用语，是以马来语为基础的东印度尼西亚接触语言。相对标准印尼语，态范畴形态消失、附加成分大幅缩减、所有者前置（sa pu rumah「我的家」），结构明显简化。Kluge（2014）将其作为独立语言而非印尼语方言处理。深受钦德拉瓦西湾地区巴布亚和南岛底层语言影响。' } };
LANG_DATA['pot'].meta = { family: 'Algic > Algonquian (Central Algonquian, Ojibwe-Potawatomi)', speakers: '~30 L1 + ~200 L2 (severely endangered; active revitalization)', countries: 'United States (Kansas, Michigan, Wisconsin, Oklahoma), Canada (Ontario)', official: 'No (heritage language of Potawatomi Nations)', script: 'Latin (modern Bodéwadmi double-vowel-derived orthography)', iso6393: 'pot', glottocode: 'pota1247', reviewStatus: 'human-reviewed', scriptTags: ['Latin'], sources: [{ type: 'reference', title: 'Hockett, Charles F. (1948) Potawatomi I-IV. International Journal of American Linguistics 14:1-10, 63-73, 139-149, 213-225.' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Lockwood, Hunter T. (2017) How the Potawatomi Language Lives: A Grammar of Potawatomi. PhD dissertation, U. Wisconsin-Madison.' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Glottolog: Potawatomi', url: 'https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/pota1247' }], description: { en: 'Potawatomi (Bodéwadmimwen, "fire-keeper language") is a Central Algonquian language closely related to Ojibwe but distinguished by systematic syncope — short unstressed vowels are deleted, producing dense consonant clusters absent in sister Anishinaabe languages. It is undergoing active revitalization by the Citizen, Prairie Band, Hannahville, Pokagon, and Walpole Island communities.', ja: 'ポタワトミ語（ボデワドミムウェン、「火の番人の言葉」）はオジブウェ語に近い中部アルゴンキン諸語の一つだが、系統的な音節脱落（短い無強勢母音の脱落）により、姉妹言語アニシナーベ諸語には見られない密な子音連結を生み出す点で区別される。複数のポタワトミ部族コミュニティで活発な言語復興運動が行われている。', ko: '포타와토미어(보데와드미므웬, "불 지키는 자의 말")는 오지브웨어와 가까운 중부 알공킨어계 언어이지만, 체계적인 단모음 탈락 현상으로 인해 자매 언어인 아니시나베어들에는 없는 조밀한 자음 연쇄가 발생하는 점에서 구별된다. 여러 포타와토미 부족 공동체에서 활발한 언어 부흥 운동이 진행 중이다.', zh: '波塔瓦托米语（Bodéwadmimwen，"守火者之语"）是与奥吉布瓦语关系密切的中部阿尔冈昆语系语言，但因系统性的音节脱落（短促非重读元音的删除）而产生姊妹阿尼希纳贝语所没有的密集辅音连缀，因此与之区分。多个波塔瓦托米部落社区正在积极推进语言复兴。' } };
LANG_DATA['uun'].meta = { family: 'Austronesian (Formosan, Western Plains)', speakers: 'Dormant (~0 L1; last L1 speaker Pan Jin-yu died 2010); revival efforts', countries: 'Taiwan (Puli, Nantou; Miaoli)', official: 'No (recognized as Plains Aboriginal heritage language; not among 16 officially recognized Taiwanese Indigenous languages)', script: 'Latin (revival orthography)', iso6393: 'uun', glottocode: 'kulo1237', dataStatus: 'fragmentary', reviewStatus: 'human-reviewed', scriptTags: ['Latin'], unattestedReason: { love: 'unsourced', hello: 'unsourced', thanks: 'unsourced', good: 'unsourced', cat: 'unsourced' }, sources: [{ type: 'reference', title: 'Li, Paul Jen-kuei & Shigeru Tsuchida (2001/2002) Pazih Dictionary. Institute of Linguistics, Academia Sinica, Taipei.' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Li, Paul Jen-kuei & Shigeru Tsuchida (2002) Pazih Texts and Songs. Institute of Linguistics, Academia Sinica.' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Lin Ying-chin (2000) A Reference Grammar of Pazih. Academia Sinica.' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Glottolog: Kulon-Pazeh', url: 'https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/kulo1237' }], description: { en: 'Kulon-Pazeh is a dormant Formosan language of the Western Plains group, spoken in central Taiwan around Puli (Nantou). Its last fully fluent L1 speaker, Pan Jin-yu, died in 2010 at age 96; community-led revival efforts continue. Notable for retaining the Proto-Austronesian alveolar/retroflex contrast and a productive Ca-reduplication pattern.', ja: 'クーロン・パゼヘ語は台湾中部・埔里周辺で話されていた西部平埔群のフォルモサ諸語で、現在は休眠言語。最後のL1話者潘金玉氏が2010年に96歳で死去し、現在は復興運動が進行中。古オーストロネシア語の歯茎・そり舌対立や生産的なCa重複を保持。', ko: '쿨론-파제흐어는 대만 중부 푸리(난터우) 일대에서 쓰이던 서부평원군의 포르모사 언어로, 현재 휴면 언어이다. 마지막 모어 화자 판진위(2010년 96세 사망) 이후 부족 주도 부활 운동이 이어진다. 원오스트로네시아어의 치경/권설 대립과 Ca-중복형을 보존한 점이 특징.', zh: '巴宰語（噶哈巫–巴宰）為台灣中部埔里一帶西部平埔群之福爾摩沙語言，現已休眠。最後一位母語使用者潘金玉於2010年以96歲高齡逝世，社群仍持續推動復振。特色為保留原南島語齒齦／捲舌對立及生產性Ca-重疊構詞。' } };
LANG_DATA['wch'].meta = { family: 'Caddoan (Northern Caddoan)', speakers: '~3 L1 (critically endangered; last fluent speaker Doris McLemore d. 2016, sleeping/dormant)', countries: 'United States (Oklahoma)', official: 'No (tribal heritage language of the Wichita and Affiliated Tribes)', script: 'Latin (linguistic orthography with ʔ and ː)', iso6393: 'wic', glottocode: 'wich1260', dataStatus: 'fragmentary', reviewStatus: 'human-reviewed', scriptTags: ['Latin'], unattestedReason: { moon: 'unsourced', love: 'unsourced', cat: 'unsourced', thanks: 'unsourced', good: 'unsourced' }, sources: [{ type: 'reference', title: 'Rood, David S. (1976) Wichita Grammar. New York: Garland.' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Rood, David S. (1975) The Implications of Wichita Phonology. Language 51(2):315-337.' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Glottolog: Wichita', url: 'https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/wich1260' }], description: { en: 'Wichita is a Northern Caddoan language of Oklahoma famous for lacking a bilabial stop /p/ entirely — a typologically extreme rarity worldwide. Its polysynthetic verbs can express whole sentences in a single word, and a glottal stop ʔ and long vowels are phonemically contrastive.', ja: 'ウィチタ語はオクラホマの北カドー諸語で、両唇閉鎖音/p/を完全に欠くことで世界的にも極めて稀な言語として知られる。多総合的動詞は一語で文全体を表現でき、声門閉鎖音ʔと長母音が音素として対立する。', ko: '위치타어는 오클라호마의 북부 카도어계 언어로, 양순 폐쇄음 /p/가 완전히 결여된 것으로 세계적으로도 극히 드문 언어이다. 다종합적 동사는 한 단어로 문장 전체를 표현할 수 있으며, 성문 폐쇄음 ʔ과 장모음이 음소로 대립한다.', zh: '威奇托语是俄克拉荷马州的北卡多语系语言，以完全缺失双唇塞音/p/而闻名——这在世界语言中极为罕见。其多式综合动词可用一个词表达整句话，喉塞音ʔ与长元音构成音位对立。' } };
LANG_DATA['wuu_jh'].meta = { family: 'Sinitic (Wu, Wuzhou 婺州片)', speakers: '~2M', countries: 'China (Jinhua, central Zhejiang)', official: 'No (regional)', script: 'Han characters', iso6393: 'wuu', glottocode: 'jinh1234', reviewStatus: 'human-reviewed', scriptTags: ['Han'], parentCode: 'wuu', dataStatus: 'fragmentary', unattestedReason: { love: 'unsourced — Jinhua dialect lexicons do not list an abstract noun form distinct from the Wu generic 爱; surface form unverified for this variety' }, sources: [{ type: 'reference', title: 'Cao Zhiyun 曹志耘 (1996) 金华方言词典 [Dictionary of the Jinhua dialect], Jiangsu Education Press (现代汉语方言大词典 series)' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Fu Guotong 傅國通 et al. (1985) 浙江吴语分区 [Subgrouping of Zhejiang Wu], 方言 1985-1' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Glottolog: Jinhua', url: 'https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/jinh1234' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Norman (1988) Chinese', url: 'https://www.cambridge.org/' }], description: { en: 'Jinhua Wu (金华话) is the prototypical representative of the Wuzhou Wu subgroup (婺州片), a primary branch of Wu Chinese coordinate with — not subordinate to — Taihu Wu (Shanghai, Suzhou, Hangzhou). It is spoken by ~2M in central Zhejiang, in the basin of the Jinhua River. Wuzhou Wu is typologically conservative: it preserves the full medieval Chinese three-way obstruent contrast (voiceless / aspirated / voiced) like other Wu groups, but its tone system (typically 7–8 categories with distinctive contour shapes) and several lexical items (e.g. 1sg pronoun 我 [ŋo], 3sg 渠 [gɛ]) differ markedly from Taihu Wu, reflecting the early branching of Wuzhou from the rest of Wu. The region is the home of the famous Jinhua ham and was the birthplace of the Song-dynasty Neo-Confucian scholar Lü Zuqian.', ja: '金華呉語（金华话）は呉語婺州片を代表する変種で、婺州片は呉語の一次分枝であり、太湖呉語（上海・蘇州・杭州）に従属するものではなく並列する。浙江省中部の金華江盆地に約200万人の話者を持つ。婺州呉語は類型的に保守的であり、他の呉語と同様に中古漢語の3項対立する阻害音系列（無声／有気／有声）を保持するが、その声調体系（典型的に7-8調で独特な声調形）や一部の語彙項目（1人称代名詞 我 [ŋo]、3人称 渠 [gɛ] など）は太湖呉語と顕著に異なり、これは婺州片が呉語の他の系統から早期に分岐したことを反映している。金華地域は有名な金華ハム（金華火腿）の産地であり、宋代の朱子学者・呂祖謙の出身地でもある。', ko: '진화 우어(金华话)는 우어 무저우편(婺州片)을 대표하는 변종으로, 무저우편은 우어의 일차 분지이며 태호 우어(상하이·쑤저우·항저우)에 종속되지 않고 병렬한다. 저장성 중부 진화강 유역에 약 200만 명의 화자를 가진다. 무저우 우어는 유형론적으로 보수적이다: 다른 우어와 마찬가지로 중고한어의 3항 대립 장애음 계열(무성·유기·유성)을 보존하지만, 성조 체계(전형적으로 7-8개의 독특한 성조형)와 일부 어휘 항목(1인칭 대명사 我 [ŋo], 3인칭 渠 [gɛ] 등)은 태호 우어와 뚜렷이 다르며, 이는 무저우편이 우어의 다른 계통에서 일찍 분지했음을 반영한다. 진화는 유명한 진화 햄(金华火腿)의 산지이며, 송대 성리학자 여조겸의 고향이기도 하다.', zh: '金华话是吴语婺州片的代表性方言，婺州片是吴语的一级分支，与太湖吴语（上海、苏州、杭州）平行而非从属。分布于浙江中部金华江流域，使用人口约200万。婺州吴语在类型上较为保守：与其他吴语一样保留中古汉语的三分阻塞音对立（清-送气-浊），但其声调体系（通常7-8调，调形别具特色）和若干词汇项（如第一人称代词 我 [ŋo]、第三人称 渠 [gɛ]）与太湖吴语差异显著，反映了婺州片自吴语早期即与其他分支分化。金华是著名的金华火腿之乡，亦为宋代理学家吕祖谦的故乡。' } };
LANG_DATA['wuu_jx'].meta = { family: 'Sinitic (Wu, Taihu / Suhujia 苏沪嘉)', speakers: '~4.5M', countries: 'China (Jiaxing, northern Zhejiang)', official: 'No (regional)', script: 'Han characters', iso6393: 'wuu', glottocode: 'jiax1234', reviewStatus: 'human-reviewed', scriptTags: ['Han'], parentCode: 'wuu', sources: [{ type: 'reference', title: 'Bao Houxing 鮑士杰 / 颜逸明 (1994) 吴语概说 [Outline of Wu Chinese], East China Normal University Press' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Qian Nairong 錢乃榮 (1992) 当代吴语研究 [Studies on contemporary Wu], Shanghai Education Press (Jiaxing chapter)' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Glottolog: Jiaxing', url: 'https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/jiax1234' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Norman (1988) Chinese', url: 'https://www.cambridge.org/' }], description: { en: 'Jiaxing Wu (嘉兴话) is a Taihu Wu variety of the Suhujia (Suzhou-Shanghai-Jiaxing) sub-cluster, spoken by ~4.5M in the city of Jiaxing in northern Zhejiang, geographically and linguistically transitional between Shanghainese to the north and Hangzhou Wu to the southwest. Like all Taihu Wu varieties, it preserves the medieval Chinese three-way obstruent contrast (voiceless–aspirated–voiced: p / pʰ / b), an archaic feature lost in Mandarin and Cantonese, with 7 contrastive tones and elaborate phrasal sandhi. Jiaxing was a major silk and grain center of the Lower Yangtze and was the birthplace of the Chinese Communist Party (1921, Nanhu).', ja: '嘉興呉語（嘉兴话）は太湖呉語の蘇滬嘉（蘇州・上海・嘉興）下位群に属する変種で、浙江省北部の嘉興市に約450万人の話者を持ち、北の上海語と南西の杭州呉語の地理的・言語的中間に位置する。すべての太湖呉語と同様に、中古漢語の3項対立する阻害音系列（無声・有気・有声：p / pʰ / b）を保持しており、これは北京語や広東語では失われた古層特徴である。7つの対立声調と精緻な句単位連声変化を持つ。嘉興は長江下流の重要な絹・穀物集散地であり、中国共産党の結党地（1921年、南湖）でもある。', ko: '자싱 우어(嘉兴话)는 태호 우어 쑤후자(쑤저우·상하이·자싱) 하위군에 속하는 변종으로, 저장성 북부 자싱시에 약 450만 명의 화자를 가지며 북쪽 상하이 우어와 남서쪽 항저우 우어 사이의 지리적·언어적 과도지대에 위치한다. 모든 태호 우어와 마찬가지로 중고한어의 3항 대립 장애음 계열(무성·유기·유성: p / pʰ / b)을 보존하며, 이는 표준 중국어와 광둥어에서 사라진 고층 특징이다. 7개의 대립 성조와 정교한 구 단위 연성변화를 가진다. 자싱은 양쯔강 하류 지역의 중요한 비단·곡물 집산지였으며, 중국공산당 창당지(1921년 난후)이기도 하다.', zh: '嘉兴话属太湖吴语苏沪嘉（苏州-上海-嘉兴）小片，分布于浙江北部嘉兴市，使用人口约450万，地理与语言上均介于北面的上海话和西南的杭州吴语之间，呈过渡型。与所有太湖吴语一样，保留中古汉语的三分阻塞音对立（清-送气-浊：p / pʰ / b），这是普通话与粤语已失的古老层位特征。具有7个对立声调和精细的连读变调。嘉兴是长江下游重要的丝绸与粮食集散地，亦为中国共产党的创建地（1921年南湖）。' } };
LANG_DATA['yue_zs'].meta = { family: 'Sino-Tibetan (Sinitic, Yue, Yuehai)', speakers: '~1.5M', countries: 'China (Zhongshan, Guangdong, Pearl River Delta)', official: 'No (regional vernacular)', script: 'Han characters', iso6393: 'yue', glottocode: 'yuee1236', reviewStatus: 'human-reviewed', scriptTags: ['Hans'], sources: [{ type: 'reference', title: 'Zhan Bohui 詹伯慧 (2002) 广东粤方言概要 [Outline of Guangdong Yue Dialects]. Jinan University Press.' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Wikipedia: Zhongshan Cantonese', url: 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zhongshan_Cantonese' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Glottolog: Yuehai', url: 'https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/yuee1236' }], description: { en: 'Zhongshan Yue (中山白话) is a Yuehai-branch Cantonese variety spoken by ~1.5M in Zhongshan prefecture on the western Pearl River Delta — the hometown speech of Sun Yat-sen. It is largely mutually intelligible with Guangzhou Cantonese but preserves a distinct Shiqi (石岐) sub-variety with slightly more conservative finals (notably retaining the -m coda contrast and a few archaic readings). Zhongshan also contains Min Nan enclaves (Longdu Min) inherited from Fujianese migration — making the prefecture itself linguistically heterogeneous despite the prestige "Shiqi vernacular" anchoring this entry.', ja: '中山白話（Zhongshan Yue）は珠江デルタ西岸の中山市で約150万人が話す粤海系広東語の変種で、孫文の故郷の言語でもある。広州広東語とほぼ相互理解可能だが、独自の石岐方言を保ち、終子音-mの対立など若干保守的な韻尾を残す。中山市内には福建移民由来の閩南語飛び地（隆都閩南語）もあり、地域全体としては言語的に多様であるが、本項目はその威信形である「石岐話」を基準とする。', ko: '중산백화（Zhongshan Yue, 中山白话）는 광둥성 주강 삼각주 서안 중산시에서 약 150만 명이 사용하는 월해계 광동어 변종으로, 쑨원(孫文)의 고향 언어이다. 광저우 광동어와 거의 상호 소통 가능하지만 독자적인 스치(石岐) 하위방언을 보존하며 -m 종성 대립 등 약간 보수적인 운미를 유지한다. 중산시 내에는 푸젠 이민에서 유래한 민난어 飛び地（룽두 민난어）도 있어 지역 전체로는 언어적으로 다양하나, 본 항목은 위신형인 「스치 백화」를 기준으로 한다.', zh: '中山白话（粤语中山片）是粤海系广东话的一种，主要通行于珠江三角洲西岸的中山市，使用者约150万——同时也是孙中山先生的乡音。与广州话基本互通，但保留独特的石岐次方言，韵尾系统略保守（如保留-m韵尾对立及若干存古读）。中山市内尚有源自福建移民的闽南语方言岛（隆都闽南语），全市语言情况实属混杂；本词条以威信形「石岐话」为准。' } };
LANG_DATA['zh_cd'].meta = { family: 'Sinitic (Mandarin, Southwestern — Cheng-Yu)', speakers: '~20M (Chengdu city + plain)', countries: 'China (Sichuan: Chengdu Plain)', official: 'No (regional vernacular; Putonghua is official)', script: 'Han characters (Simplified)', iso6393: 'cmn', glottocode: 'sich1238', reviewStatus: 'human-reviewed', scriptTags: ['Han'], parentCode: 'zh', sources: [{ type: 'reference', title: 'Zhang Yisheng 张一生 (1995) 成都话音系研究 (A Phonological Study of Chengdu Dialect), 四川大学出版社' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Liang Deman 梁德曼 (1982) 成都方言词典 (Chengdu Dialect Dictionary), 江苏教育出版社' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Norman, Jerry (1988) Chinese, Cambridge University Press', url: 'https://www.cambridge.org/' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Glottolog: Sichuan Mandarin', url: 'https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/sich1238' }], description: { en: 'Chengdu Mandarin (成都话) is the prestige variety of Southwestern Mandarin spoken on the Chengdu Plain by ~20M people, and the urban core of the broader Sichuanese (Cheng-Yu) cluster. Its 4-tone system (yinping ˥, yangping ˨˩, shangsheng ˥˧, qusheng ˨˩˧) sits in a notably lower pitch register than Beijing Mandarin, and it has merged historical /n-/ and /l-/ initials (so 男 nán and 蓝 lán are homophones nan˨˩). The Middle Chinese entering tone (rusheng) has lost its glottal stop coda but is reassigned as a single category — distinct from Beijing, which redistributed rusheng across all four tones. Chengdu is the medium of teahouse banter (摆龙门阵 bai-long-men-zhen), sketch comedy (谐剧), and a famously laid-back urban culture.', ja: '成都話（成都话）は西南官話の威信変種で、成都平原で約2,000万人に話され、より広範な四川（成渝）方言群の都市核となる。4声調体系（陰平 ˥、陽平 ˨˩、上声 ˥˧、去声 ˨˩˧）は北京官話よりも音域が顕著に低く、歴史的な /n-/ と /l-/ の頭子音は合流している（男 nán と藍 lán が同音 nan˨˩）。中古漢語の入声は喉門閉鎖韻尾を失ったが、北京官話のように四声へ分散せず単一の声調カテゴリーとして残存している点が特徴。成都話は茶館での「擺龍門陣」、諧劇、ゆったりした都市文化の媒体である。', ko: '청두말(成都话)은 서남관화의 위신 변종으로 청두 평원에서 약 2,000만 명이 사용하며, 더 넓은 쓰촨(成渝) 방언군의 도시 핵심을 이룬다. 4성조 체계(음평 ˥, 양평 ˨˩, 상성 ˥˧, 거성 ˨˩˧)는 베이징 관화보다 음역이 현저히 낮고, 역사적 /n-/ 와 /l-/ 두자음이 합류하여 男 nán과 藍 lán이 동음(nan˨˩)이 된다. 중고한어 입성은 성문 폐쇄 종성을 잃었으나 베이징처럼 4성으로 흩어지지 않고 단일 성조 범주로 보존된다. 청두말은 찻집의 「바이룽먼전(擺龍門陣)」 만담, 해극(諧劇), 느긋한 도시 문화의 매개이다.', zh: '成都话是西南官话的威望变体，通行于成都平原，使用人口约2,000万，是更大范围的四川（成渝）方言群的都市核心。其4声调系统（阴平 ˥、阳平 ˨˩、上声 ˥˧、去声 ˨˩˧）音域明显低于北京官话，且历史上的 /n-/ 与 /l-/ 声母合流（男 nán 与 蓝 lán 同音 nan˨˩）。中古汉语入声虽然丢失喉塞韵尾，却未像北京话那样分派入四声，而是合并为一个独立调类。成都话是茶馆「摆龙门阵」、谐剧及悠闲都市文化的载体。' } };
LANG_DATA['zh_hf'].meta = { family: 'Sinitic (Mandarin, Jianghuai / Hongchao 洪巢片)', speakers: '~5M', countries: 'China (Hefei urban area, central Anhui)', official: 'No (regional; standard Mandarin is official)', script: 'Han characters', iso6393: 'cmn', glottocode: 'hefe1240', reviewStatus: 'human-reviewed', scriptTags: ['Han'], parentCode: 'zh_jh', sources: [{ type: 'reference', title: 'Li Rong 李榮 et al. (1987–1998) 中國語言地圖集 [Language Atlas of China], Longman / Commercial Press' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Kong Huifang 孔慧芳 (2011) 合肥方言研究 [Studies on the Hefei dialect], Anhui University Press' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Glottolog: Hefei', url: 'https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/hefe1240' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Norman (1988) Chinese', url: 'https://www.cambridge.org/' }], description: { en: 'Hefei (合肥话) is a Jianghuai Mandarin variety of the Hongchao subgroup, spoken by ~5M in the capital of Anhui province. Like other Jianghuai varieties (Nanjing, Yangzhou), it preserves the medieval Chinese entering tone (入声) as a short syllable ending in a glottal stop [ʔ] — a feature lost in all of the Northern Mandarin heartland. It also exhibits the characteristic Jianghuai merger of /n/ and /l/ initials, and a 5-tone system (yin-ping, yang-ping, shang, qu, ru). Hefei sits at the interface between Mandarin to the north and Wu to the south, on the historical Huai River boundary.', ja: '合肥話（合肥话）は江淮官話洪巢片に属する変種で、安徽省の省都に約500万人の話者を持つ。他の江淮官話（南京、揚州）と同様に、中古漢語の入声を声門閉鎖音 [ʔ] で終わる短音節として保持しており、これは北方官話の中心地ではすべて失われた特徴である。江淮官話に特徴的な /n/ と /l/ 声母の合流を示し、5声調体系（陰平・陽平・上・去・入）を持つ。合肥は北の官話と南の呉語の境界、すなわち歴史的な淮河境界線上に位置する。', ko: '허페이 방언(合肥话)은 강회관화 홍소편에 속하는 변종으로, 안후이성의 성도에 약 500만 명의 화자를 가진다. 다른 강회관화(난징·양저우)와 마찬가지로, 중고한어의 입성(入声)을 성문폐쇄음 [ʔ]로 끝나는 단음절로 보존하며, 이는 북방관화 중심지에서 모두 소실된 특징이다. 강회관화 특유의 /n/과 /l/ 성모 합류를 보이며, 5성조 체계(음평·양평·상·거·입)를 가진다. 허페이는 북쪽 관화와 남쪽 우어의 경계, 곧 역사적인 화이허 경계선 위에 자리한다.', zh: '合肥话属江淮官话洪巢片，分布于安徽省省会合肥市区，使用人口约500万。与其他江淮官话（南京、扬州）相同，保留了中古汉语的入声，以喉塞音 [ʔ] 收尾的促声形式呈现——这是北方官话核心区已完全消失的特征。同时呈现江淮官话典型的 n/l 声母合流，具有5个声调（阴平、阳平、上、去、入）。合肥地处北方官话与南方吴语的交界线上，即历史上的淮河分界线。' } };
LANG_DATA['zh_kf'].meta = { family: 'Sinitic (Mandarin, Zhongyuan — Zheng-Cao)', speakers: '~5M (Kaifeng city + prefecture)', countries: 'China (Henan: Kaifeng)', official: 'No (regional; Putonghua is official)', script: 'Han characters (Simplified)', iso6393: 'cmn', glottocode: 'zhon1235', reviewStatus: 'human-reviewed', scriptTags: ['Han'], parentCode: 'zh', sources: [{ type: 'reference', title: 'He Wei 贺巍 (1989) 开封方言志 (Kaifeng Dialect Gazetteer), 语文出版社' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'He Wei 贺巍 (2005) 中原官话分区(稿) (A Proposed Sub-Classification of Zhongyuan Mandarin), 方言 2005.2' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Norman, Jerry (1988) Chinese, Cambridge University Press', url: 'https://www.cambridge.org/' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Glottolog: Zhongyuan Mandarin', url: 'https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/zhon1235' }], description: { en: 'Kaifeng Mandarin (开封话) is a Zheng-Cao subgroup variety of Zhongyuan (Central Plains) Mandarin spoken by ~5M people in and around Kaifeng, Henan. Kaifeng was the capital of the Northern Song dynasty (960–1127) — the largest city in the world at the time — and its speech preserves an important early-Mandarin stratum: the historical Middle Chinese entering tone (rusheng) has merged into yinping ˨˦ for voiceless initials (unlike Beijing, where rusheng dispersed across all four tones), and the 4-tone system (yinping ˨˦, yangping ˦˨, shangsheng ˥˧, qusheng ˧˩˨) is shared in broad outline with Zhengzhou and other Zhongyuan dialects. Like other Henan varieties it preserves the /tsʰ/-/tʂʰ/ distinction less rigidly than Standard Mandarin and has a productive diminutive 儿 -er suffix (轻声 light tone).', ja: '開封話（开封话）は中原官話・鄭曹片の変種で、河南省開封市とその周辺で約500万人に話される。開封は北宋（960–1127）の首都であり、当時世界最大の都市の一つであった。開封話は初期官話の重要な層を保持しており、中古漢語の入声（rusheng）は無声声母の場合、北京話のように四声に分散せず一律に陰平 ˨˦ に合流する。4声調体系（陰平 ˨˦、陽平 ˦˨、上声 ˥˧、去声 ˧˩˨）は鄭州など他の中原官話と概ね共有される。標準官話に比して /tsʰ/ と /tʂʰ/ の対立はやや緩く、儿（-er、軽声）による指小辞が生産的に用いられる。', ko: '카이펑말(开封话)은 중원관화 정조편(郑曹片)에 속하는 변종으로 허난성 카이펑시와 그 주변에서 약 500만 명이 사용한다. 카이펑은 북송(960–1127)의 수도였으며, 당시 세계 최대 도시 중 하나였다. 카이펑말은 초기 관화의 중요한 층위를 보존하고 있어, 중고한어 입성(rusheng)은 무성 성모의 경우 베이징처럼 사성에 분산되지 않고 일률적으로 음평 ˨˦에 합류한다. 4성조 체계(음평 ˨˦, 양평 ˦˨, 상성 ˥˧, 거성 ˧˩˨)는 정저우 등 다른 중원관화와 대체로 공유된다. 표준 관화에 비해 /tsʰ/와 /tʂʰ/의 대립이 다소 느슨하며, 儿(-er, 경성)을 통한 지소사가 생산적으로 사용된다.', zh: '开封话是中原官话郑曹片的代表变体，通行于河南省开封市及其周边地区，使用人口约500万。开封是北宋（960–1127）的都城，当时为世界最大城市之一，其方言保留了早期官话的重要层次：中古汉语入声（rusheng）在清声母字中合流入阴平 ˨˦，而非如北京话分派入四声。4声调系统（阴平 ˨˦、阳平 ˦˨、上声 ˥˧、去声 ˧˩˨）与郑州等其他中原官话大体一致。与普通话相比，开封话 /tsʰ/ 与 /tʂʰ/ 的对立较松，儿尾（-er，轻声）作为指小词缀使用十分活跃。' } };
LANG_DATA['zh_nj'].meta = { family: 'Sinitic (Mandarin, Jianghuai — Hong-Chao)', speakers: '~6M (Nanjing city + Jiangning, Liuhe)', countries: 'China (Jiangsu: Nanjing metropolitan area)', official: 'No (regional; Putonghua is official). Historically the de facto court koine of the Ming and early Qing.', script: 'Han characters (Simplified)', iso6393: 'cmn', glottocode: 'nanj1234', reviewStatus: 'human-reviewed', scriptTags: ['Han'], parentCode: 'zh', sources: [{ type: 'reference', title: 'Liu Danqing 刘丹青 (1995) 南京方言词典 (Nanjing Dialect Dictionary), 江苏教育出版社 (in the 现代汉语方言大词典 series ed. Li Rong)' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Bao Mingwei 鲍明炜 (1998) 南京方言志 (Nanjing Dialect Gazetteer), 南京出版社' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Coblin, W. South (2000) "A brief history of Mandarin", Journal of the American Oriental Society 120', url: 'https://www.jstor.org/' }, { type: 'reference', title: 'Glottolog: Nanjing', url: 'https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/nanj1234' }], description: { en: 'Nanjing Mandarin (南京话) is the urban-prestige variety of Jianghuai Mandarin spoken by ~6M people in greater Nanjing, and one of the most historically prestigious Chinese vernaculars: it served as the de facto national koine (官話 Guanhua) of the Ming and early Qing courts, was the basis of the "Mandarin" recorded by Matteo Ricci and Jesuit missionaries in the 17th century, and remained the standard pronunciation taught in late-Qing schoolbooks until Beijing-based Putonghua displaced it in the 1920s–30s. Phonologically Nanjing preserves the Middle Chinese entering tone (rusheng, ~˥ʔ) — lost in northern Mandarin but shared with Wu and Hui — and lacks the /n-/ ~ /l-/ merger typical of southwestern Mandarin. Its 5-tone system (˧˩, ˩˧, ˨˩˨, ˦, ˥ʔ) makes it transitional between Mandarin and Wu.', ja: '南京話（南京话）は江淮官話の都市威信変種で、南京都市圏で約600万人に話され、中国諸方言の中でも歴史的に最も威信の高い口語の一つである：明代および清初の宮廷において事実上の全国通語（官話）として機能し、17世紀のマテオ・リッチらイエズス会宣教師が記録した「マンダリン」の基底となり、清末の学校教科書では北京基盤の普通話に取って代わられる1920–30年代まで標準発音として教えられていた。音韻的には中古漢語の入声（rusheng、約 ˥ʔ）を保持し──北方官話では消失したが呉語・徽語と共有する特徴──西南官話に典型的な /n-/ と /l-/ の合流を示さない。5声調体系（˧˩、˩˧、˨˩˨、˦、˥ʔ）は官話と呉語の過渡的位置を示している。', ko: '난징말(南京话)은 강회관화의 도시 위신 변종으로 난징 도시권에서 약 600만 명이 사용하며, 중국 방언 가운데 역사적으로 가장 위신이 높은 구어 중 하나이다: 명대와 청 초의 궁정에서 사실상의 전국 통용어(官話)로 기능하였고, 17세기 마테오 리치 등 예수회 선교사들이 기록한 「만다린」의 기초가 되었으며, 청말 학교 교과서에서는 1920–30년대 베이징 기반 푸퉁화로 대체되기 전까지 표준 발음으로 교수되었다. 음운적으로는 중고한어 입성(rusheng, 약 ˥ʔ)을 보존하며 — 북방관화에서는 소실되었으나 우어·후이어와 공유되는 특징 — 서남관화에 전형적인 /n-/ ~ /l-/ 합류는 나타나지 않는다. 5성조 체계(˧˩, ˩˧, ˨˩˨, ˦, ˥ʔ)는 관화와 우어의 과도적 위치를 보여준다.', zh: '南京话是江淮官话的都市威望变体，通行于南京都市圈，使用人口约600万，是汉语方言中历史上威望最高的口语之一：在明代及清初的宫廷中实际上为全国通语（官话），是17世纪利玛窦等耶稣会传教士所记录之「Mandarin」的基底，并在清末学校课本中作为标准发音教学，直至1920–30年代被以北京音为基础的普通话所取代。音韵上保留中古汉语入声（rusheng，约 ˥ʔ）——北方官话已失，但与吴语、徽语共享——且不存在西南官话典型的 /n-/ 与 /l-/ 合流。其5声调体系（˧˩、˩˧、˨˩˨、˦、˥ʔ）显示出官话与吴语之间的过渡地位。' } };

LANG_DATA['nl_be'].meta = { family:'Germanic', speakers:'~6.5M', countries:'Belgium (Flanders)', official:'Belgium (Dutch is co-official)', script:'Latin', parentCode:'nl', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'Belgian Dutch (Vlaams / Flemish) is the variety of Dutch spoken in Flanders, Belgium (~6.5M speakers). It shares the standard written language and spelling with Netherlands Dutch but differs notably in pronunciation: a soft velar/palatal g [ɣ~ʝ] (vs the harsh northern [χ]), an alveolar trill or tap r [r] (vs uvular), more monophthongal vowels, and fuller unreduced -en endings ([ən]). It is codified as standaardnederlands with Flemish pronunciation norms.', ja:'ベルギー・オランダ語（フラマン語、Vlaams）は、ベルギーのフランデレン地方で話されるオランダ語の変種で、約650万人の話者を持つ。綴り・書き言葉はオランダ（北部）と共通だが発音が顕著に異なる：柔らかい軟口蓋・硬口蓋音 g [ɣ~ʝ]（北部の硬い [χ] に対し）、歯茎ふるえ音／弾き音 r [r]（口蓋垂音でなく）、より単母音的な母音、-en 語尾を [ən] と完全に発音する点など。フラマン発音規範を持つ標準オランダ語として体系化されている。'} };
LANG_DATA['en_us'].meta = { family:'Germanic', speakers:'~230M', countries:'United States', official:'United States (de facto)', script:'Latin', parentCode:'en', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'General American (GA) is the most widely spoken accent of American English and the de-facto broadcast standard across much of the United States (~230M native speakers). Unlike the British RP reflected in the base English entry, GA is rhotic — r is pronounced in all positions (water, father, heart) — uses a flapped [ɾ] for intervocalic t/d (water, butter), and for most speakers merges the cot–caught vowels.', ja:'一般米国英語（General American, GA）はアメリカ英語で最も広く話される発音で、合衆国の多くで事実上の放送標準（母語話者約2億3千万人）。基底「英語」が反映するイギリス容認発音（RP）と異なり r音性で、語末・子音前の r も発音し（water, father, heart）、母音間の t/d を弾き音 [ɾ] にし（water, butter）、多くの話者で cot–caught 母音が融合する。'} };
LANG_DATA['en_ca'].meta = { family:'Germanic', speakers:'~28M', countries:'Canada', official:'Canada (co-official with French)', script:'Latin', parentCode:'en', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'Canadian English (~28M native speakers) is a rhotic North American variety close to General American but distinguished by Canadian Raising — /aɪ/ and /aʊ/ raise to [ʌɪ ʌʊ] before voiceless consonants, so writer and rider differ in vowel quality — and a near-universal cot–caught merger. It keeps some British spellings and lexis (colour, zed).', ja:'カナダ英語（母語話者約2,800万人）は r音性の北米変種で一般米国英語に近いが、カナダ式上げ（無声子音の前で /aɪ aʊ/ が [ʌɪ ʌʊ] に上がり、writer と rider の母音が異なる）とほぼ普遍的な cot–caught 融合で区別される。一部イギリス式の綴り・語彙（colour, zed）を保つ。'} };
LANG_DATA['en_za'].meta = { family:'Germanic', speakers:'~5M', countries:'South Africa', official:'South Africa (one of 11 official)', script:'Latin', parentCode:'en', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'South African English (~5M native, ~30M total speakers) is a non-rhotic variety and one of South Africa\'s 11 official languages. It is marked by the KIT split (central [ɪ] vs front [i]), raised TRAP and DRESS vowels, and very monophthongal long vowels, alongside loanwords from Afrikaans and Bantu languages.', ja:'南アフリカ英語（母語話者約500万人、総話者約3,000万人）は非r音性の変種で、南アフリカの11公用語の一つ。KIT 分裂（中央寄り [ɪ] と前寄り [i]）、上がった TRAP・DRESS 母音、非常に単母音的な長母音を特徴とし、アフリカーンス語やバントゥー諸語からの借用語を持つ。'} };
LANG_DATA['de_ch'].meta = { family:'Germanic', speakers:'~5M', countries:'Switzerland, Liechtenstein', official:'Switzerland, Liechtenstein', script:'Latin', parentCode:'de', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'Swiss Standard German (Schweizer Hochdeutsch) is the formal written standard of German used in German-speaking Switzerland (~5M people) — distinct from the Alemannic dialect (Swiss German, gsw) of everyday speech. One of the three national standard varieties of German, it omits the letter ß (writing ss), is more monophthongal, has a typically alveolar or uvular r, and carries French/Italian loanwords (Velo \'bicycle\', Billett \'ticket\').', ja:'スイス標準ドイツ語（Schweizer Hochdeutsch）はドイツ語圏スイス（約500万人）の正式・書記の標準ドイツ語で、日常で話されるアレマン方言（スイスドイツ語 gsw）とは別物。ドイツ語の三国家標準変種の一つで、文字 ß を用いず ss と綴り、より単母音的、r は概ね歯茎音または口蓋垂音、フランス語・イタリア語の借用語（Velo「自転車」、Billett「切符」）を持つ。'} };
LANG_DATA['pt_ao'].meta = { family:'Romance', speakers:'~17M', countries:'Angola', official:'Angola', script:'Latin', parentCode:'pt_eu', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'Angolan Portuguese (~17M speakers) is the variety of Portuguese spoken in Angola, where it is the official language and increasingly a first language in cities. Phonologically closer to European Portuguese, but under Bantu influence it reduces unstressed vowels far less — giving fuller, clearer vowels — with distinctive rhythm and vocabulary from Kimbundu, Umbundu and Kikongo.', ja:'アンゴラ・ポルトガル語（話者約1,700万人）はアンゴラで話されるポルトガル語の変種で、同国の公用語、都市部では第一言語化が進む。音韻的には欧州ポルトガル語に近いが、バントゥー諸語の影響で無強勢母音の弱化がはるかに少なく明瞭な母音を持ち、キンブンドゥ語・ウンブンドゥ語・キコンゴ語の借用語と独特のリズムを示す。'} };
LANG_DATA['es_ve'].meta = { family:'Romance', speakers:'~28M', countries:'Venezuela', official:'Venezuela', script:'Latin', parentCode:'es_mx', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'Venezuelan Spanish (~28M speakers) is a Caribbean variety of Spanish. Like other Caribbean dialects it has seseo (no /θ/), aspirates or drops syllable-final /s/ → [h] (los → [loh]), velarises word-final /n/ to [ŋ], and has yeísmo; lexicon and the voseo/tuteo mix vary by region.', ja:'ベネズエラ・スペイン語（話者約2,800万人）はカリブ系のスペイン語変種。他のカリブ方言同様、セセオ（/θ/ なし）、音節末 /s/ の帯気化・脱落 → [h]（los→[loh]）、語末 /n/ の軟口蓋化 [ŋ]、ジェイスモを持つ。語彙や voseo/tuteo の混在は地域による。'} };
LANG_DATA['ca_va'].meta = { family:'Romance', speakers:'~2.4M', countries:'Spain (Valencian Community)', official:'Spain (Valencian Community, co-official)', script:'Latin', parentCode:'ca', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'Valencian (Valencià) is the standard variety of Catalan spoken in the Valencian Community (~2.4M speakers), codified by the Acadèmia Valenciana de la Llengua. Unlike Central Catalan it does not reduce unstressed a/e to schwa (keeping clear [a] and [e]) and preserves a distinct open/closed vowel system with its own morphology and vocabulary; politically often named separately, it is linguistically a variety of Catalan.', ja:'バレンシア語（Valencià）はバレンシア州（話者約240万人）で話されるカタルーニャ語の標準変種で、バレンシア言語アカデミー（AVL）が規範を定める。中央カタルーニャ語と異なり無強勢の a/e をシュワーに弱化させず（明瞭な [a][e] を保つ）、独自の開／閉母音体系・形態・語彙を持つ。政治的には別名で呼ばれることが多いが言語学的にはカタルーニャ語の変種。'} };

LANG_DATA['es_pr'].meta = { family:'Romance', speakers:'~3.5M', countries:'Puerto Rico', official:'Spanish (co-official with English in Puerto Rico)', script:'Latin', parentCode:'es_mx', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'Puerto Rican Spanish is a Caribbean variety derived from 16th–18th century Andalusian Spanish with Canarian influences, overlaid with Taíno indigenous substrate and West African phonetic patterns. Key features: (1) Syllable-final /r/ → [l] or uvular [χ] (lambdacism/lateralization); (2) Syllable-final /s/ → [h] or zero (aspiration/deletion); (3) Intervocalic /d/ → deletion (padre [pai̯], madre [mai̯]); (4) Word-final /n/ → [ŋ] (velarization); (5) Vowel lengthening after coda /s/ deletion; (6) Fricative /x/ consistently realized as [h]; (7) Rhotics exhibit extensive variation including uvular re'} };
LANG_DATA['es_do'].meta = { family:'Romance', speakers:'~10M', countries:'Dominican Republic', official:'Dominican Republic', script:'Latin', parentCode:'es_mx', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'Dominican Spanish (es_do) is characterized by extensive syllable-final consonant weakening and deletion — particularly /s/ aspiration/deletion, /d/ deletion intervocalically and finally, /r/ reduction/deletion in word-final position (rhotacism). Shares yeísmo (ll/y merger) and seseo (s/z merger) with most Latin American Spanish varieties. Maintains velar fricative /x/ in jota contexts. The phonetic values shown reflect the educated urban Dominican Spanish (particularly Santo Domingo register). Final rhotic often deleted or lambdacized; word-final vowels sometimes nasalized. Parent variety: es_'} };
LANG_DATA['es_gt'].meta = { family:'Romance', speakers:'~16M', countries:'Guatemala', official:'yes', script:'Latin', parentCode:'es_mx', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'Guatemalan Spanish is the official language spoken by approximately 16 million people (93% of Guatemala\'s population; native speakers approximately 69% of 17.6M total). As a Central American Spanish variety, it exhibits: (1) Seseo (merger of /θ/ and /s/ as [s]), (2) Yeísmo (merger of /ʎ/ and /ʝ/ as [j]), (3) Lenition of voiced stops /b d g/ to fricatives/approximants [β̞ ð̞ ɣ̞] in intervocalic position, (4) Full consonant preservation (unlike Caribbean varieties; final /s/ is generally maintained rather than aspirated or dropped, particularly in highlands), (5) Velarization of word-final /n/ t'} };
LANG_DATA['es_ec'].meta = { family:'Romance', speakers:'~13.5M', countries:'Ecuador', official:'Official language of Ecuador', script:'Latin', parentCode:'es_mx', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'Highland (Serrano) Ecuadorian Spanish represents the conservative phonological variety spoken in the Andean mountain regions (Sierra) including Quito, Cuenca, and Ambato. This variety is characterized by: (1) Preservation of clear final /s/ (not aspirated like coastal variants), (2) Full consonant pronunciation with slower, measured pace, (3) Seseo (merger of /s/ and /θ/ into [s]), (4) Yeísmo presence (though /ʎ/ vs /ʝ/ distinction maintained in some Highland areas, particularly Loja), (5) Fricative trill realization of /r/ as [r̝] or assibilated variant, (6) Preservation of intervocalic stops'} };
LANG_DATA['es_uy'].meta = { family:'Romance', speakers:'~3.4M', countries:'Uruguay', official:'yes', script:'Latin', parentCode:'es_ar', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'Uruguayan Spanish (es_uy) is a regional variety with parent es_ar (Argentine Spanish). Part of the Rioplatense Spanish dialect continuum, spoken in Uruguay and by Uruguayan diaspora communities. Distinctive phonological features include: (1) Yeísmo rehilado — merger of /ʎ/ and /ʝ/ into a single postalveolar fricative, typically voiced [ʒ] (zheísmo) but sometimes voiceless [ʃ] (sheísmo); (2) Seseo — no phonemic distinction between /θ/ and /s/, both realized as /s/; (3) S-aspiration — /s/ frequently becomes [h] before consonants or pauses; (4) Velar /x/ is never glottalized; (5) Standard Spanish'} };
LANG_DATA['ar_sy'].meta = { family:'Semitic', speakers:'~5M', countries:'Syria', official:'No (de facto in Syria/Lebanon; parent variety ar_lev covers broader Levantine region)', script:'Latin', parentCode:'ar_lev', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'Syrian Arabic (ar_sy) is a regional variety of Levantine Arabic (ar_lev, parent code apc in ISO 639-3) spoken in Syria and by diaspora communities. It shares the phonological inventory of broader Levantine varieties with some local features: vowel shifts (ɪ/u for ا/و in casual speech), glottal stop ʔ for Quranic hamza in many contexts, pharyngeal consonants ʕ/ħ retained, and emphatic/non-emphatic consonant pairs. The IPA provided reflects Damascene/urban Syrian standards as documented in phonological studies (Cowell 1964, Al-Wer 2007). Speaker population estimates range 4-6M including diaspora'} };
LANG_DATA['ar_ye'].meta = { family:'Semitic', speakers:'~30-40M', countries:'Yemen', official:'No official status; Modern Standard Arabic used for official purposes', script:'Latin', parentCode:'ar', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'Yemeni Arabic is a cluster of conservative dialects native to Yemen, characterized by preservation of interdental fricatives and regional consonant variations. The variety shown represents Sanʽani-based pronunciation (largest speaker population ~20M). Other major dialects include Ta\'izzi-Adeni (~6.76M speakers), Hadhrami (~6M speakers), and Tihami (~3.5M speakers). Ta\'izzi-Adeni distinctively preserves Classical Arabic syllable structure by avoiding vowel deletion. Emphasis-marked consonants (indicated by superscript ˤ) trigger pharyngealization and affect vowel quality. No official status; Mo'} };
LANG_DATA['ar_dz'].meta = { family:'Semitic', speakers:'~40M', countries:'Algeria', official:'Not official; regional colloquial variety with significant second-language speakers', script:'Latin', parentCode:'ar_ma', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'Algerian Arabic (ar_dz / arq in LangMap) is a Maghrebi Arabic variety spoken primarily in Algeria, with ~40 million speakers. Phonologically characterized by emphatic consonants (ˤ), schwa reduction in short syllables, and Berber substrate influence (e.g., yəmma \'mother\' is a Berber borrowing, contrasting with Arabic ʔumm in other varieties). Notable features: palatalized /ʃ/ and /ʒ/ affrication, loss of case marking, use of perfective/imperfective aspectual distinction. The elided article /l-/ is common (e.g., lma \'the water\', ssalaːm \'the greeting\'). Emphasis ˤ marks uvular backing on adjace'} };
LANG_DATA['ar_sa'].meta = { family:'Semitic', speakers:'~14-19M', countries:'Saudi Arabia', official:'Saudi Arabia, Saudi Arabia (co-official in Iraq/Syria border regions)', script:'Latin', parentCode:'ar_gulf', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'Najdi Arabic is a major regional variety of Gulf Arabic with ~14-19 million native speakers, primarily in Saudi Arabia (Najd region including Riyadh, Qassim, and Ha\'il) plus speakers in Iraq, Syria, Jordan, and Kuwait. Key phonological features: /ɡ/ as modern reflex of historical /q/; affricates [tʃ]/[dʒ] before front vowels in northern/central dialects; emphatic pharyngealized consonants /tˤ/, /sˤ/, /dˤ/, /ðˤ/; pharyngeal fricatives /ħ/, /ʕ/; vowel system with short /a, i, u/ and long /iː, aː, uː, eː, oː/; gahawa syndrome (epenthetic /a/ after gutturals); q→g shift distinguishes Najdi from cl'} };
LANG_DATA['ar_lb'].meta = { family:'Semitic', speakers:'~5.5M', countries:'Lebanon', official:'No (vernacular; MSA &amp; French official in Lebanon)', script:'Latin', parentCode:'ar_lev', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'Lebanese Arabic (ar_lb) is the urban vernacular spoken in Lebanon, primarily in Beirut and surrounding regions. Phonetically, it is nearly identical to parent ar_lev (Levantine Arabic) in its core features: urban /ʔ/ for qāf, /ʒ/ for ǧīm, final geminate degemination in pause form, and the imāla vowel shift. The variety-specific IPA provided here matches the Beiruti urban norm documented in dialectological literature (Watson 2002, Holes 2004). Surface spellings are identical to ar_lev; no colloquial-specific spelling variants are obligatory (though Beiruti may use French orthographic influence '} };
LANG_DATA['en_wls'].meta = { family:'Germanic', speakers:'~2.8M', countries:'Wales', official:'de facto; English is co-official with Welsh in Wales', script:'Latin', parentCode:'en', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'Welsh English is the English dialect spoken in Wales. Key phonological features include: (1) Alveolar flap [ɾ] or trill [r] for /r/ under Welsh language influence; (2) Devoicing of /z, ʒ, dʒ/ especially in southern varieties; (3) H-dropping in southern varieties (Cardiff); (4) Post-stress consonant gemination/lengthening (e.g., \'jetty\' [ˈdʒɛtːiː]); (5) Preservation of distinctions like chew/choose, yew/you not found in many other English varieties; (6) Regional variation: Cardiff influenced by Hiberno-English and West Midlands; North influenced by Welsh language retention; South Valleys by Wes'} };
LANG_DATA['en_jam'].meta = { family:'Germanic', speakers:'~2.65M (Jamaica ~2.6M + diaspora ~0.05M L1; ~97% of population speaks English as L1/L2)', countries:'Jamaica', official:'Yes', script:'Latin', parentCode:'en', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'Jamaican English (en_jam) is the official language of Jamaica and a post-creole continuum variety on a spectrum from standard English to Jamaican Patois (jam). Key phonological features: (1) STRUT vowel /ʌ/ realized as [ɵ~o], more closed-rounded than RP/GA; (2) variable semi-rhoticity (r-sounds context-dependent: preserved in stressed final positions, dropped before consonants or in unstressed syllables); (3) absence of central schwa reduction—unreduced vowels appear where RP uses /ə/, instead using [a~ɐ] or retaining full vowels; (4) /aʊ/ diphthong more closed [oʊ~ɵʊ]; (5) potential cot–caugh'} };
LANG_DATA['en_ng'].meta = { family:'Germanic', speakers:'~60M"', countries:'Nigeria', official:'Yes (official language of Nigeria)', script:'Latin', parentCode:'en', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'Nigerian English is characterized by: (1) VOWEL SYSTEM: 7-10 pure vowels instead of RP\'s 13, with mergers of tense-lax vowel pairs (/i:/−/ɪ/, /u:/−/ʊ/); /ʌ/ typically realized as /ɔ/ or /a/ (Hausa influenced); /æ/ realized as /a/. (2) DIPHTHONGS: Monophthongization of /aɪ/ /aʊ/ /ɔɪ/ /eɪ/ common in mesolectal speech; diphthongs may reduce to long monophthongs. (3) CONSONANTS: Dental fricatives /θ/ /ð/ typically become /t/ /d/ (southern varieties) or /s/ /z/ (Hausa varieties); final consonants often unreleased; consonant clusters simplified. (4) PROSODY: Tonal characteristics similar to West Afr'} };
LANG_DATA['en_ph'].meta = { family:'Germanic', speakers:'~110M', countries:'Philippines', official:'yes', script:'Latin', parentCode:'en', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'Philippine English (en_PH) is an official regional variety spoken in the Philippines, with approximately 110 million speakers (native and non-native combined). It exhibits features of a non-rhotic accent with British English influences in formal contexts and American English influences in informal speech. The variety shows distinctive phonological characteristics including: (1) Non-rhoticity with optional schwa-coloring of pre-consonantal and word-final /r/; (2) Merger of /ɔ/ and /ɑː/ in many contexts, reflected in pronunciation like "dog" as [dɔg] and "water" as [ˈwɔːtə]; (3) Clear-l and dark'} };
LANG_DATA['en_ke'].meta = { family:'Germanic', speakers:'~3M', countries:'Kenya', official:'yes', script:'Latin', parentCode:'en', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'Kenyan English is an English variety spoken as a second language by approximately 2.7-3 million speakers in Kenya. It is one of Kenya\'s two official languages (alongside Swahili). The variety is heavily influenced by Swahili and Bantu substrate languages (Kikuyu, Luhya) and Nilotic languages (Dholuo). Key phonological features include: (1) Simplified five-vowel system (/a/, /e/, /i/, /o/, /u/) based on Swahili, with monophthongization of English diphthongs; (2) Loss of vowel length contrast; (3) Retention of full vowel articulation in unstressed syllables rather than reduction to schwa (e.g., '} };
LANG_DATA['fr_sn'].meta = { family:'Romance', speakers:'~5M', countries:'Senegal', official:'yes', script:'Latin', parentCode:'fr', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'Senegalese French is the official language variety of Senegal. Key phonological features distinguishing it from Standard Metropolitan French include: (1) Alveolar trill [r] instead of the standard uvular fricative [ʁ], (2) Very prominent nasal vowels characteristic of African French, (3) Marked intonation patterns with word-initial stress followed by falling pitch, (4) Rhythmic elements from Wolof influence creating distinctive prosodic features. The variety shows minimal lexical divergence from Standard French in formal registers, though colloquial speech features borrowings from Wolof and ot'} };
LANG_DATA['fr_ci'].meta = { family:'Romance', speakers:'~3-5M (L1 and L2 combined in Côte d\'Ivoire)', countries:'Côte d\'Ivoire', official:'Official language in Côte d\'Ivoire', script:'Latin', parentCode:'fr', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'fr_ci (Ivorian French) is not currently implemented as a separate entry in the langmap codebase. The project contains a pan-African `fr_af` (African French) aggregate anchored to neutral West African educated French. Ivorian-specific features (Nouchi street register, regional phonology adaptations) are deliberately excluded from the base fr_af dataset. Ivorian French differs from metropolitan French in: (1) contact features from local languages (especially Akan/Twi, Mandinka, Kru languages); (2) Nouchi vocabulary and code-mixing in urban registers; (3) slightly reduced schwa in unstressed syll'} };
LANG_DATA['fr_ht'].meta = { family:'Romance', speakers:'~4.5M', countries:'Haiti', official:'Yes', script:'Latin', parentCode:'fr', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'Haitian French is a regional variety of French spoken in Haiti, distinct from Haitian Creole. Key phonological features: (1) The uvular fricative /ʁ/ is realized as [ɣ] (voiced velar fricative) and frequently becomes silent in syllable coda position, particularly before consonants or prosodic breaks. (2) Nasal vowels show slight variations from Metropolitan French: /ɑ̃/ → [ã], /ɔ̃/ → [õ], /œ̃/ → [œ̃]. (3) Distinctive intonation influenced by Haitian Creole substrate. (4) Official status: French is an official language of Haiti (co-official with Haitian Creole), though only 5-20% of the populat'} };
LANG_DATA['pt_mz'].meta = { family:'Romance', speakers:'~3M', countries:'Mozambique', official:'Mozambique', script:'Latin', parentCode:'pt_eu', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'Mozambican Portuguese (Português de Moçambique) is the variety spoken in Mozambique by ~3M people as an official language. It shares the European Portuguese phonological base but with influences from local Bantu languages and patterns similar to other African Portuguese varieties. The phonetic realizations provided closely follow the European Portuguese parent system (pt_eu) documented in linguistic sources, with some regional variation in vowel and consonant realizational patterns influenced by substrate languages. The variety maintains the characteristic European Portuguese features includin'} };
LANG_DATA['pt_cv'].meta = { family:'Romance', speakers:'~500k', countries:'Cape Verde', official:'yes', script:'Latin', parentCode:'pt_eu', codeType:'regional-variant', scriptTags:['Latin'], description:{en:'Cape Verdean Portuguese is a regional variety spoken in Cape Verde and is the official language alongside Cape Verdean Creole (the national language and mother tongue). Key phonetic features distinguishing it from European Portuguese include: (1) laminal dental /l/ [l̄], articulated with the blade of the tongue touching the upper teeth, contrasting with European Portuguese\'s velarized alveolar [u026b]; (2) greater reduction of unstressed vowels, particularly /a/ realized as [aɐ] in pre-tonic positions; (3) deletion of some unstressed high vowels [i, u, ɨ] by speakers from the northern islands,'} };

LANG_DATA["adx"].meta = { family:"Sino-Tibetan (Bodish)", speakers:"800,000–1.8 million (Ethnologue/Glottolog estimates; 2020 census ~1.86 million ethnic Tibe", countries:"", official:"Language of recognized nationality in China (PRC); used in education and media in Tibetan-majority areas; no official status outsi", script:"Tibetan script (Uchen/dbu-can abugida, derived from Brahmi via Indian ", scriptTags:['Latin'], dataStatus:'fragmentary', description:{en:"Sources: Wiktionary Amdo Tibetan Swadesh list (Yang 2017, Southwest Minzu University dissertation); Glottolog 5.3 (amdo1237); Wikipedia Amdo Tibetan; Ethnologue (adx); Wikivoyage Amdo Tibetan phrasebook; Wikidata Q56509. Geographic center (lat/lng) based on Xining, Qinghai (36.6255°N, 101.7574°E), a major Amdo Tibetan-speaking center. Vocabulary primarily from Yang (2017) Swadesh list with IPA transcriptions reflecting Aba dialect phonology. Four-vowel system (/e, ə, a, o/); nomad dialects prese [Provisional - limited documentation; readings pending native-speaker verification.]"} };
LANG_DATA["qxs"].meta = { family:"Sino-Tibetan (Qiangic)", speakers:"approximately 800-1500 speakers", countries:"", official:"not official; minority language status in Aba Tibetan and Qiang Autonomous Prefecture, Sichuan", script:"unwritten; typically romanized via pinyin or represented in Hanzi", scriptTags:['Latin'], dataStatus:'fragmentary', description:{en:"Data confidence: LOW (QXS is critically under-documented). Geographic coordinates (32.8°N, 103.6°E) place the center in Aba Tibetan and Qiang Autonomous Prefecture, Sichuan Province, China. Vocabulary items drawn from comparative Qiangic reconstruction and Northern Qiang (CND) cognates per LaPolla & Huang (2003) \"A Grammar of Qiang\" — direct Southern Qiang attestations are scarce in published sources. IPA reflects likely Qiangic phonological patterns (uvular/postalveolar affricates, aspirated st [Provisional - limited documentation; readings pending native-speaker verification.]"} };
